apital Inc. is a business development company specializing in term loans, equipment financing, and private equity-related investments. The firm provides tech lending, equipment financing, life sciences, warehouse lending, and sponsor finance sources. The firm is industry agnostic and invests in growth-stage companies across industries, including aerospace, software, Agricultural Equipment, Alternative Protein, Clean Technology, Energy, Food and Beverage / CPG, Information Technology, Life Sciences, Oil and Gas, Robotics, Semiconductors, Transportation, and consumer and retail. They provide investors with stable and consistent returns through access to the private credit market. Trinity Capital Inc. was founded in 2008 and is based in Phoenix, Arizona, with additional offices in Solana Beach, California and San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kyle Steven Brown | CEO, President, Chief Investment Officer & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 113 people. Stock-based compensation of $107K per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["Trinity Capital Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.8B market cap.","Accruals are elevated at +27.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","Net dilution runs at 5.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 3.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +27.0% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \